#heading(level: 2)[#text("An explicit invariant generating family")]

#text("Let b_​k=z^k, k=0..359, and d_​k be its trace-dual basis. Exact binary linear algebra computes d_​k; native checks verify129,600 trace-pairing entries,360 separability-idempotent sums and64 direct trace controls. For each of the twelve chart coordinates f, retain the circuit")

#block(inset: 5pt)[#set text(size: 8pt)
#raw("I_(f,k)=sum_(j=0..359) rho^j(b_k*f),\nrho^j(f)(P)=sigma^j(f(alpha^(-j)(P))),\nf=sum_(k=0..359) d_k*I_(f,k).", block: true)]

#text("The rho orbit sum is fixed, and the idempotent identity gives recovery. This supplies4,320 possibly redundant rational generators per quotient, not4,320 algebraically independent coordinates. The constant extension of the field generated by these invariants recovers the original function field. Galois descent supplies the fixed-field interpretation; see the written proof and ")#link("https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CDQ")[#text("Stacks Galois descent")]#text(". Trace duality uses the nondegenerate separable trace pairing described in ")#link("https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BIE")[#text("Stacks trace and norm")]#text(".")

#text("All360 weights are evaluated for x0,y0,z0,z1 at one fixture per graph: 5,760 invariant values,16 exact coordinate recoveries and128 equivariance controls pass, with1,440 additional point steps. At a general K-point, the correct identity is I(alpha(P))=I(P)^2. Its value need not belong toF2. The universal recovery formula applies to all twelve functions; only the four specified coordinate families are evaluated in this point control. No invariant polynomial relation ideal or saturation has been computed.")

#heading(level: 2)[#text("Bounded lower-genus quotient diagnostic")]

#text("Test five diagonal twists g^u and five reflections g^j R, for both traces: 50 signed controls on the known augmentation component. Here g=D^2, R D R=D^-1 and D R D^-1=g R. Twisted Frobenius on that component is D^(2u+1) tensor the elliptic Frobenius companion.")

#text("A reflection is stable exactly when2u+1=0 mod5, hence u=2. That twist collapses the known component to E_​t^4; its reflection-fixed part has polynomial(E_​t)^2 and dimension2. The other twists retain the known four-dimensional A5 component but no tested reflection is stable. Thus zero of50 controls gives both properties. Exact integer characteristic polynomials and all commutators are checked. This does not exclude A5 in other Jacobian factors, or other lower-genus carrier families.")

#text("The carrier genus is2841. Conditional Riemann-Hurwitz arithmetic gives reflection-quotient genus≤1421; its actual genus, ramification and equations are not computed. The inequality is proved in Lean with its hypothesis.")

